/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:31:01-08:00","id":40958,"title":"","content":"For Werewolf fight scenes, I play Joe Satriani, amongst others.<br /> For creepy, find a music player that can slow down / speed up the music, slow it way down, and put on some dubstep. Great WTF--Creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:54:58-08:00","id":40968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40658-the-soundtrack-score-music-thread?p=40941#post40941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything by Midnight Syndicate. I have a playlist of all kinds of music for casual RP. But I want spooky ambient I go with MS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used Midnight Syndicate as THE soundtrack for my Victorian Age: Mage game. Great stuff.<br /> For my Werewolf: Rednecks! game I used a lot of contemporary country music like Toby Keith, Dwight Yoakam and Clint Black.<br /> My Dark Ages game gets a mixed treatment depending on the mood:<br /> -For dark moments and the umbra I use a selection of Lustmord tracks.<br /> -For the caern scenes and surrounding forests I use the Adiemus album &quot;The eternal knot&quot;.<br /> -For battle I use tracks from groups like Two Steps from Hell or E.S. Posthumus.<br /> -I also use single tracks or small combinations for places/characters, like gregorian chants for the local monastery etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:36:49-08:00","id":41071,"title":"","content":"Let's try something different from the usual mantra of Goth and Punk music, so here's my list of theme songs for each of the 13 Clans and the Nine Traditions as well, all from various genres.<br /> <br /> Here we go...<br /> <br /> Vampire Clans<ul><li>Brujah: Breaking The Law-Judas Priest</li> <li>Gangrel: Wild Side-Motley Crue</li> <li>Malkavian: Where Is My Mind?-The Pixies</li> <li>Nosferatu: The Monster Mash-Bobby Boris Pickett</li> <li>Toreador: Puttin' On The Ritz-Taco</li> <li>Tremere: It's a Kind of Magic-Queen</li> <li>Ventrue: It's All About The Benjamins-Puff Daddy</li> <li>Lasombra: The Sound of Silence-Simon &amp; Garfunkel</li> <li>Tzimisce: Dragula-Rob Zombie</li> <li>Assamite: Hunter-Yade</li> <li>Followers of Set: Straight to Hell-Hank Williams III</li> <li>Giovanni: Speak Softly Love-Andy Williams</li> <li>Ravnos: Gypsies, Tramps, and Thieves-Cher</li> </ul><br /> Mage Traditions<ul><li>Akashic Brotherhood: Kung-Fu Fighting-Carl Douglas</li> <li>Celestial Chorus: Spirit in the Sky-Norman Greenbaum</li> <li>Cult of Ecstasy: White Rabbit-Jefferson Airplane</li> <li>Dreamspeakers: Run to the Hills-Iron Maiden</li> <li>Euthanatos: Death Metal-Possessed</li> <li>Order of Hermes: Abracadabra-The Steve Miller Band</li> <li>Verbena: Pagan Fears-Mayhem</li> <li>Sons of Ether: Hangar 18-Megadeth</li> <li>Virtual Adepts: It's All About the Pentiums-Weird Al Yankovic</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}